==============================================================================
M46 b4 -- question 120: is the sb=0 censoring SPECTRAL LEAKAGE?
==============================================================================

1. THE LEAKAGE FLOOR, measured with no modelling assumption.
   `bandlimited` has EXACTLY ZERO Fourier power above 0.20 cyc/px.
   Ring power measured at 0.45 cyc/px is therefore leakage, 100%.
   Reported as dB below the peak ring; noiseless, so nothing else
   can be putting power there.

   window      P(0.45)/P_peak      dB      P(0.45)/P(0.20)
   rect             1.0208e-16   -159.9       8.2287e-16
   hann             1.3806e-14   -138.6       1.6002e-13
   blackman         2.0760e-15   -146.8       2.5393e-14
   bharris          1.2440e-16   -159.1       1.5608e-15
   hann+pre9        3.6330e-14   -134.4

2. DOES THE LEAKED POWER CARRY FALSE CORRELATION?
   Two independent noisy captures of the BAND-LIMITED latent.  Above
   0.20 cyc/px the only true correlation is the fixed pattern; every
   other correlated thing up there is leaked from below the cutoff.
   TRUE FRC above the cutoff, with FPN excluded, is 0 by construction.

   no_FPN:   window       FRC(0.45)   FRC(0.2762)   crossing
              rect           +0.0043       -0.0040   0.2058           
              hann           +0.0181       +0.0095   0.2058           
              blackman       +0.0160       +0.0119   0.2076           
              bharris        +0.0135       +0.0124   0.2122           
              hann+pre9      +0.0180       +0.0072   0.2059           

